Subject: Cantor SJS Repository Graph P0 Justification

@ [justification_uuid] f7248cf6-ad90-4beb-9bf5-ab04165433c3
@ [canonical_uuid] 3c7435a1-a5ae-44f1-a32b-a92741a7ec91

& [Claim]
  + a pure independently joined change-set verifier is the smallest executable seam that makes whole-graph Git custody and per-element justification mechanically meaningful without inventing mutation authority

& [Support]
  + Cantor already stores the SJS layers but recent commit bodies lack direct graph pointers and no universal change-set coverage verifier exists
  + signed Pinky governance requires stable element history typed edges and exact staged-delta coverage
  + existing cantor_ecosystem patterns prove strict supplied-form validation canonical digests replay and adversarial denial with no dependency delta
  + B1 physical update preflight remains selection-gated while this provider-free seam is unblocked and directly supports every future governed commit

& [AlternativesRejected]
  + documentation-only adoption cannot mechanically refuse missing or invented element history
  + trusting a change set's embedded path list is self-attestation rather than independent coverage
  + invoking Git inside P0 silently crosses into physical host and process authority
  + line-number identity loses continuity under refactoring
  + code-comment duplication pollutes implementation and still lacks typed source proof and frontier edges
  + repository-wide historical rewrite violates immutable correction history

& [Decision]
  + authorize only the exact pure validator bounded file-input CLI fixtures evidence and no-dependency surface after signature
  + leave actual staged inventory acquisition hook enforcement commit and push to later authority
